      <h1 id="configuring-request-header-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring a request header identity provider<a href="#configuring-request-header-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Configure the <code>request-header</code> identity provider to identify users from request header values, such as <code>X-Remote-User</code>. It is typically used in combination with an authenticating proxy, which sets the request header value.</p>
      <h2 id="identity-provider-overview_configuring-request-header-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Identity providers in OpenShift Container Platform<a href="#identity-provider-overview_configuring-request-header-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can configure identity providers by creating a custom resource (CR) that describes the provider and adding it to the cluster. Identity providers enable user authentication in OpenShift Container Platform beyond the default <code>kubeadmin</code> user.</p>
