      <h2 id="identity-provider-about-request-header_configuring-request-header-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">About request header authentication<a href="#identity-provider-about-request-header_configuring-request-header-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>A request header identity provider identifies users from request header values, such as <code>X-Remote-User</code>. It is typically used in combination with an authenticating proxy, which sets the request header value. The request header identity provider cannot be combined with other identity providers that use direct password logins, such as htpasswd, Keystone, LDAP or basic authentication.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
